// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row format_arg_unrenderable_form_refused (tier 3, `refuses`).
// The format family expands by RENDERING each argument back to source and
// re-parsing the block; an argument whose AST form render_expr_src cannot
// spell is refused —
//     println!: argument 0 is an expression form the format expansion cannot
//     carry yet (AST code …); bind it to a local first
// Rust prints `5`. Until 2026-09-24 such an argument rendered as a comment and
// printed NOTHING (`(f)(1)`, a closure call, `format!`/`vec!` arguments — those
// forms are rendered now and pinned by pass/format_args_render_every_callee);
// the refusal replaced the silent wrong output for what is left: the loop and
// jump forms, comprehensions, chained comparisons, quotes, metacalls.
// The root is the render-and-reparse design, not a missing case: each case
// added closes one spelling. The fix that closes the class carries the lowered
// argument rather than its text.
package format_arg_unrenderable_form_refused;
use logos.std.fmt;
fn main() -> i32 {
    println!("{}", loop { break 5i64; });
    return 0i32;
}
